 transformers. Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria (doc `utility-capex-2027`).\n- **Data centres:** Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than 2026 because power availability limits new sites (doc `datacentre-demand`). Demand is still growing, but the pace is slowing.\n- **Customer concentration:** Utilities are 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Pellham is 35% of those utility orders and Norvane is 21%. VLTX is therefore mostly exposed to the two utilities with the strongest capex growth (doc `vltx-order-mix`). Because Pellham is so large, one customer's plans or delays could move the picture.\n- **Financing (not my question):** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, and equity markets have been less receptive (doc `utility-credit`). I only saw the snippet of that document. Whether the capex plans can be funded is the question n3 is working on.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- These are plans and expectations, not orders or backlog.\n- I found no order-book or backlog series.\n- The sources give no data on equipment lead times or pricing.","ttft_ms":2584,"type":"result","duration_ms":17888,"uuid":"a9654610-a896-420d-b878-4042e6228f3b","ttft_stream_ms":1886,"time_to_request_ms":791,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":102,"system_prompt":45,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":14,"input_attachments":79,"input_hooks":11,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":57,"tool_pool_refresh":111,"init_message":69,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":32,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":47,"request_announcements":84,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":26,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":40,"request_build":68},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":490,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":98,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":170,"process_anon_mib_turn